    "created_at": "2017-01-10T21:39:16Z",
    "updated_at": "2017-01-10T21:39:16Z",
    "body": "> I don't think we'd need to change the parser to ignore `<plaintext>` (and doing so would break the xss mitigations like Safen Up that I noted above).\r\n\r\nI meant only `<plaintext>` token \"in select\" -- not in general. But I see now that this is already the case! So the attack you describe doesn't work already.\r\n\r\nhttp://software.hixie.ch/utilities/js/live-dom-viewer/saved/4781\r\n\r\n> Anything else\r\n> Parse error. Ignore the token.\r\n\r\nhttps://html.spec.whatwg.org/#parsing-main-inselect",
    "author_association": "MEMBER",
    "pin": null,
